<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pange lingua gloriosi corporis mysterium</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Pange lingua gloriosi corporis mysterium&quot; is a medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> hymn attributed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-aquinas">Thomas Aquinas</a> (1225–1274), written for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corpus-christi-feast">Feast of Corpus Christi</a>. It is also sung on Maundy Thursday, during the procession that carries the Blessed Sacrament from the church to the place where it is kept until Good Friday.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>&quot;<b>Pange lingua gloriosi corporis mysterium</b>&quot; is a medieval Latin hymn attributed to Thomas Aquinas (1225–1274), written for the Feast of Corpus Christi.</blockquote><a href="/songs/pange-lingua-gloriosi-corporis-mysterium">Pange lingua gloriosi corporis mysterium</a></li></ul></section>
